{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>והיה</b> — the sense of אחפש בנרות (I will search with lamps), for by a lamp a person can see what is in the innermost chambers, for the light of the sun does not enter there. And thus: נר אלהים נשמת אדם (the lamp of Elohim is the soul of man) חופש (searching); and בנרות is as though: בנרות אחפשם (with lamps I will search them)." "<b>הקופאים</b> — who are complacent and quiet." "<b>ומלת קופאים</b> — like קפאו תהומות (the deeps froze). A thing that dwells and is gathered together is called קפאון. And thus קופאים are those who dwell securely in their place."], :book :zephaniah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Zephaniah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/zfanya"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:47:16.426981788Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}